Description: framework for developing visual-novel type games - Android support
 Ren'Py is a programming language and runtime, intended to ease the creation
 of visual-novel type games. It contains features that make it easy to
 display thoughts, dialogue, and menus; to display images to the user; to
 write game logic; and to support the saving and loading of games.
 .
 This package installs the upstream Ren'Py 8.3.4 RAPT (Ren'Py Android
 Packaging Tool) files under /usr/share/games/renpy/rapt so the Debian
 Ren'Py launcher can build Android packages. The Android SDK is expected
 at /usr/lib/android-sdk from the google-android-*-installer packages.
 Gradle working copies are written to ~/.cache/renpy-rapt.

